# Files excluded from the EAS Build upload archive.
#
# EAS_NO_VCS=1 archives the WORKING DIRECTORY (so uncommitted work ships without a commit),
# which means anything sitting in the project root gets uploaded unless it is listed here.
# `.agents/skills` is ~10MB of agent tooling that Metro never bundles; it took the upload
# from 2.1MB to 12.1MB and contributes nothing to the APK.
.agents/
graphify-out/

# Build outputs and scratch
dist/
dist-*/
.expo/

# Docs and reference material
*.md
!README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⚠️ THIS FILE REPLACES .gitignore FOR THE EAS ARCHIVE — it does not add to it.
# eas-cli reads .gitignore ONLY when this file is absent (vcs/local.js,
# initIgnoreAsync early-returns as soon as .easignore exists). So anything git
# ignores but this file does not list IS STILL UPLOADED. That is how
# e2e/artifacts — 338 MB of Playwright videos and traces — rode along in every
# build until 2026-08-31: the archive was 347 MB for a ~9 MB project.
# Measured, not assumed: replicate the filter with Ignore.createForCopyingAsync
# from eas-cli's own vcs/local.js before believing a size claim here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The Phase 18 Playwright E2E harness. Never bundled into the APK (tsconfig
# excludes it, eslint ignores e2e/**, Vitest is scoped to src/), so excluding
# the whole directory is safe — and e2e/artifacts alone is 338 MB of run output.
e2e/
test-results/
playwright-report/
.playwright/

# Owner scratch recordings in the repo root (~3.4 MB). The app bundles no audio
# assets, so nothing in src/ can reference these.
/*.mp3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 SECRETS. These are all in .gitignore — and that is NOT enough, because of
# the rule stated above: .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for the archive. A
# gitignored secret sitting in the working tree is uploaded to EAS on every
# build unless it is ALSO listed here. Measured 2026-08-31: five gitignored
# files were in the archive, four of them secret — both Android signing
# keystores, the plaintext keystore/key passwords, and the Firebase FCM V1
# service-account private key.
#
# Why it matters even though EAS already holds the keystore: the build archive
# is a separate artifact with its own retention and download path, it is
# extracted on a build worker, and the FCM service-account key is NOT something
# EAS holds in this form — it belongs only in `eas credentials`.
#
# ⚠️ IF YOU ADD A SECRET PATTERN TO .gitignore, ADD IT HERE TOO.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
credentials.json
credentials/
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
*.mobileprovision
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
google-service-account*.json
.env*.local

# Voice probe captures
e2e/voice-probe/
